cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Retrieval-Successor Retention"
abstract: >-
  Retrieval-Successor Retention (RSR) replaces Thought Gestalt's oldest-first
  working-memory eviction with a learned policy that evicts the slot with the
  lowest predicted future retrieval demand, to test whether a system trained
  only to predict the next sentence rediscovers Kintsch and van Dijk's (1978)
  leading-edge retention strategy.
authors:
  - family-names: Keane
    given-names: Brendan
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Keanooo7/retrieval-successor-retention"
url: "https://github.com/Keanooo7/retrieval-successor-retention"
keywords:
  - working memory
  - memory eviction
  - recurrent transformer
  - discourse comprehension
  - cognitive modelling
